// title: Who switched on the direct management API or touched its access keys (AzureActivity, 90 days)
// date: 2026-11-24
// product: Sentinel
// tables: AzureActivity
// purpose: Threat Research: Azure API Management Classic: secrets stored in APIM read through a management-plane flaw (fixed 19 Nov 2026)
// source: https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/microsoft-azure-flaw-exploited-to-steal-customers-api-credentials/
// kind: incident-note
// author: Threat Research analysis (the morning analysis)
// archived by tools/kql_archive.py (CLAUDE.md 5l, 5eu)
// APIM Classic secrets (Nov 2026): tenant access = the direct management API switch and its keys
// Microsoft.ApiManagement/service/tenant: write (enable), listSecrets (read keys), regenerate*Key
AzureActivity
| where TimeGenerated > ago(90d)
| where ResourceProviderValue =~ "MICROSOFT.APIMANAGEMENT"
| extend Op = tolower(OperationNameValue)
| where Op endswith "/tenant/write" or Op contains "/tenant/listsecrets" or Op contains "/tenant/regenerate"
| summarize Count = count(), First = min(TimeGenerated), Last = max(TimeGenerated),
            Ops = make_set(Op, 10), IPs = make_set(CallerIpAddress, 20), Status = make_set(ActivityStatusValue, 5)
    by Caller, _ResourceId
| order by First asc
